://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":21110,"digest":"sha256:73e3e2cf92e0bbf06c4c26b6383e1499decb8810334a2b30d1ec8899b18aeb8b","download_count":4664,"created_at":"2026-11-03T18:02:13Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T18:02:14Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/releases/download/v1.29.2/packslip.sigstore.json"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/releases/assets/706569161","id":706569161,"node_id":"RA_kwDOT-nLJc4qHWPJ","name":"SHA256SUMS","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":705,"digest":"sha256:2955e2bfe461810eea12571b132cef91046948aea87dac03701939ee67071fba","download_count":149,"created_at":"2026-11-03T18:01:35Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T18:01:36Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/releases/download/v1.29.2/SHA256SUMS"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/tarball/v1.29.2","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/zipball/v1.29.2","body":"Compile errors in build-script-generated files now show real paths instead of mbx placeholders. macOS builds started right after you save or check out a file no longer fail with a spurious \"compiler input was modified\" error.\n\n## Fixed\n\n- **Compile errors show real paths for build script `OUT_DIR`** ([#897](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/pull/897), @jdx). When a compile error pointed into a build script's `OUT_DIR`, `cargo build` through mbx printed mbx's placeholder (`--> ${out_dir}/gen.rs:1:29`) instead of the file's path, even on a cold cache. The same happened in `--message-format=json` output, which also broke trybuild `compile_fail` snapshots. Cache hits already showed real paths. Now mbx also rewrites rustc's stdout and stderr back to real paths during live compiles, so the output matches plain Cargo. Escaping stays valid in JSON diagnostics. The same applies to other mapped roots such as `${target}`, and to `${workspace}` when `MBX_SHARE_WORKSPACE_ROOT` is on. Cache entries still store the placeholder form, so sharing across checkouts works as before.\n- **macOS builds survive metadata writes during compilation** ([#894](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/pull/894), @ViRb3). macOS adds extended attributes such as `com.apple.provenance` to a file about 1 to 2 seconds after an app writes it. If a build started in that window, mbx threw away rustc's result with `compilation result was discarded: compiler input was modified during compilation`, and every dependent crate failed with `extern location ... does not exist` until you built again. Now, if only an input's change time moves while its length, modification time and file identity stay the same, the build succeeds and that compilation is not cached. mbx records it as an `InputMetadataChangedDuringCompilation` bypass. Any other change to the input still discards the result.\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/compare/v1.29.1...v1.29.2","mentions_count":2}